<title>INDIA: India BSE shifts scrips to specified share section.</title>
<headline>India BSE shifts scrips to specified share section.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) on Friday said it would include 20 shares in its specified or A group of shares effective February 24.</p>
<p>Specified shares are actively traded and liquid stocks.</p>
<p>The shares are Asea Brown Boveri, Tata Hydro Electric Power Supply Company, Crompton Greaves, Lakme, Bharat Forge, Ceat, Videocon International, Gujarat State Fertilisers &amp; Chemicals, Hero Honda Motors, Essar Steel, SPIC, Garware Polyesters, Reckitt &amp; Colman of India, Gujarat Alkalies &amp; Chemicals, Nagarjuna Fertilizers &amp; Chemicals, Mastershare, Garware Wall Ropes, Esab India, Excel Industries and SmithKline Beecham Pharma India.</p>
</text>
